# 3. NON-NEGOTIABLE ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES

Follow these principles throughout development:

1. Security must be designed into the system from the beginning.
2. Financial transactions must be traceable and auditable.
3. No posted financial transaction may be silently edited or deleted.
4. All money calculations must use exact decimal arithmetic.
5. All important operations must be transactional and idempotent.
6. No payment must be treated as successful merely because a request was sent.
7. No mobile-money webhook must be trusted without verification.
8. No sensitive operation may rely only on a phone number.
9. Offline data must not automatically become financially confirmed data.
10. No critical feature may rely on hardcoded sample data in production.
11. Every important operation must have appropriate authorization.
12. Database backups and tested recovery procedures are mandatory.
13. The system must be usable on low-end Android smartphones and unreliable networks.
14. Do not build microservices prematurely.
15. Do not sacrifice financial correctness for development speed.

Use clean architecture principles, domain-driven design where useful, separation of concerns and modular boundaries.

Prefer simple, understandable implementations over unnecessary abstraction.

