# 22. CYBERSECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Treat security as a first-class engineering discipline.

Implement:

AUTHENTICATION:
- Secure password hashing using Argon2id or an appropriate maintained equivalent.
- Strong password policy.
- MFA for privileged users.
- Secure session handling.
- Short-lived access tokens where JWT is used.
- Refresh token rotation and revocation.
- Login rate limiting.
- Account lockout or progressive throttling.
- Secure password reset.
- Session expiry.
- Device/session management.

AUTHORIZATION:
- Deny by default.
- Server-side role and resource checks.
- Hub-level data isolation.
- No reliance on frontend permission checks.
- Separation of duties.

APPLICATION SECURITY:
- Validate all input.
- Parameterised database queries.
- Protect against SQL injection.
- Protect against XSS.
- Protect against CSRF where applicable.
- Restrict CORS.
